Title: The Lighthouse
Credit: a play by

# ACT ONE

## The Lamp Room

= Edda climbs to the lamp room to find the light already burning.

The lamp room of a decommissioned lighthouse. Dusk. EDDA, 60s, enters carrying a toolbox she clearly doesn't need.

EDDA
Someone's been up here.

## The Ledger

= The keeper's ledger holds an entry dated tomorrow.

Same room, later. Edda holds an open ledger to the lamplight.

EDDA
(reading)
"Relieved at last. All's well."
(beat)
That's my handwriting.
